Forces `hipcc` to locate `rocm_agent_enumerator` using the EasyBuild environment variable
instead of relying on a monolithic ROCm path.

Original issue: The `hipcc` C++ binary (`hipBin_amd.h`) hardcodes its search path for
`rocm_agent_enumerator` based on a unified `$ROCM_PATH` (typically `/opt/rocm`). In an
EasyBuild/EESSI environment, ROCm components are decoupled into separate modular directories.
Consequently, `hipcc` fails to find `rocm_agent_enumerator` (from `rocminfo`), breaking
downstream compilations that need GPU target detection.

Note: Unlike ROCm 6.x which used Perl scripts, ROCm 7.2.3 hipcc is fully C++-based.
The HIP_CLANG_PATH is already properly read from environment variables in hipBin_base.h,
so only the rocm_agent_enumerator path needs to be patched.

Author: Jan André Reuter <j.reuter@fz-juelich.de>
Author: Sreenivasa Murthy Kolam <sreenivasamurthy.kolam@amd.com>

--- llvm-project-rocm-7.2.3/amd/hipcc/src/hipBin_amd.h.orig	2025-02-26 22:42:00.000000000 +0530
+++ llvm-project-rocm-7.2.3/amd/hipcc/src/hipBin_amd.h	2025-08-05 12:00:00.000000000 +0530
@@ -782,7 +782,8 @@
     } else if (os != windows) {
       // Else try using rocm_agent_enumerator
       string ROCM_AGENT_ENUM;
-      ROCM_AGENT_ENUM = roccmPath + "/bin/rocm_agent_enumerator";
+      // Use EBROOTROCMINFO environment variable set by EasyBuild's rocminfo module
+      ROCM_AGENT_ENUM = string(getenv("EBROOTROCMINFO")) + "/bin/rocm_agent_enumerator";
       targetsStr = ROCM_AGENT_ENUM +" -t GPU";
       SystemCmdOut sysOut = hipBinUtilPtr_->exec(targetsStr.c_str());
       regex toReplace("\n+");
